cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this atlas, or any of the anatomical data in it, please cite it as
  below. The numbers carry their own primary sources on every card; please cite
  those as well where you rely on them.
title: Microalgae 3D Atlas
abstract: >-
  An interactive 3D cell atlas of microalgae and cyanobacteria, drawn from
  primary sources and stating the provenance of every measurement. The first
  specimen is Spirulina (Limnospira platensis), from the helical trichome under
  transmitted light down to a nanometre-scale cutaway of one cell. Each of the
  19 clickable structures carries dated dimensions marked at one of three
  confidence tiers — measured in Spirulina itself, taken from model
  cyanobacteria, or not yet established — so a reader can tell what is known
  from what is inferred. The constraints those numbers have to satisfy are
  asserted in code rather than left as prose.
type: software
